<p>The GPQA-Diamond gap (70.2 vs 86+) is exactly what the Parametric Compression-Coverage Hypothesis predicts — knowledge-intensive tasks remain harder for compact models. But on every verifiable reasoning benchmark, VibeThinker-3B matches or exceeds models 100–300× larger. The IFEval score of 93.4 confirms that extreme reasoning optimization doesn't compromise instruction following either.</p>
<p>The paper's conclusion: <strong>compact models are not merely deployment-efficient substitutes — they are a complementary research trajectory</strong>. Verifiable reasoning can be pushed very far within 3B parameters when training focuses on the right problems, with the right algorithm, and verification is pushed to test time.</p>
</section>

