    <p>The training uses a four-stage Spectrum-to-Signal pipeline: broad supervised fine-tuning across domains, a hard-reasoning SFT phase focused on long traces and high error-rate problems, multi-domain reinforcement learning using MGPO (which focuses gradient updates on problems where the model is right about 50% of the time — exactly at its capability boundary), and offline self-distillation. At test time, Claim-Level Reliability Assessment samples 32 trajectories, extracts 5 key logical claims from each, has the model self-verify those claims, and selects the answer with the highest reliability-weighted support. This raises AIME26 from 94.3 to 97.1 without any model updates.</p>
